> But do you *necessarily* see a clover, or is it merely a possibility 
> (just like receiving an artifact)? I was under the impression that, given 
> the right circumstances, you *might* receive a clover, you *might* 
> receive an artifact, or you *might* simply see your offering "consumed in 
> a burst of flame" without any other message.

There are two specific reasons the last case might occur:

* your luck is already maxed
* the corpse is below the threshold difficulty value to earn you a
  luck bonus.

Only monsters with difficulty 4 or greater will earn you a clover when
sacrificed; the difficulty is irrelevant for receiving an artifact.

> (And I don't recall ever seeing a clover on the same sacrifice as being 
> granted an artifact.)

These are two exclusive possibilities.

